---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
---
<ContentLayout title="Privacy Policy | StackGeist" description="How StackGeist handles information, hosting data, affiliate links, and third-party services.">
  <div class="legal-page">
    <p class="page-kicker">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">This policy describes what StackGeist currently collects, what third parties may process, and what changes would require an update.</p>
    <p class="effective">Effective August 16, 2026</p>
    <div class="legal-body">
      <section><h2>Information StackGeist currently collects</h2><p>StackGeist does not currently offer user accounts, comments, a newsletter, or a contact form. We do not currently run first-party analytics or advertising trackers on the site.</p><p>If those features are added later, this policy will be updated before or when they are enabled.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Hosting and security data</h2><p>StackGeist is hosted through Cloudflare. Like most hosting and security providers, Cloudflare may process technical request data such as IP addresses, browser information, timestamps, requested URLs, and security-related information needed to deliver and protect the site.</p><p>Cloudflare's handling of that information is governed by its own privacy terms.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Affiliate and external links</h2><p>Some StackGeist pages contain affiliate links to Amazon or links to other manufacturers and retailers. When you follow an external link, that third party may collect information, set cookies, or otherwise process your activity under its own privacy policy.</p><p>StackGeist does not control the privacy practices of those external sites.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Cookies</h2><p>StackGeist does not currently set first-party analytics or advertising cookies. Third-party sites you visit through outbound links may use their own cookies or similar technologies.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Children's privacy</h2><p>StackGeist is a general-audience setup and gear publication. It is not designed to collect personal information from children, and the site currently has no feature intended to collect personal information from visitors.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>This policy will be revised when StackGeist adds material data-collection features, analytics, advertising technology, forms, newsletters, or other services that change how visitor information is handled.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Questions</h2><p>See the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> for the current contact status. StackGeist does not currently collect messages through the website.</p></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</ContentLayout>
